# Certificate distribution table.
#
# One line per domain. Adding a new domain to the system is a one-line change
# here — distribute-certs.sh, the renewal checker and the restart applier all
# read this file, and nothing else needs to know about the new domain.
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated):
#   domain      the certbot lineage name (as under /etc/letsencrypt/live/<domain>)
#   dest        directory that receives the certificate
#   owner:group ownership applied to the copied files
#   format      split    -> fullchain.pem (0644) + privkey.pem (0640) in dest
#               combined -> dest/<domain>.pem containing fullchain + privkey
#               both     -> split files AND the combined PEM
#   service     which service must be restarted/reloaded when this cert changes
#               (haproxy | rsyslog | tunnel | none)
#
# HAProxy note: its `crt` directive is pointed at /etc/certs/proxy/combined/,
# and it loads *every file* in that directory. Per-domain subdirectories must
# therefore live outside it, which is why split copies go to
# /etc/certs/proxy/<domain>/ while the combined PEM goes one level up in
# combined/. Do not point HAProxy at a directory containing subdirectories.

# domain                     dest                              owner:group      format    service
#ntfy.example.com            /etc/certs/proxy/ntfy             root:haproxy     both      haproxy
#rss.example.com             /etc/certs/proxy/rss              root:haproxy     both      haproxy
#watch.example.com           /etc/certs/proxy/watch            root:haproxy     both      haproxy
#checks.example.com          /etc/certs/proxy/checks           root:haproxy     both      haproxy
#a.tunnel.example.com        /etc/certs/tunnel/a               root:tunnel      split     tunnel
#b.tunnel.example.com        /etc/certs/tunnel/b               root:tunnel      split     tunnel
